# Vulnerabilities accepted for the blocking Trivy scan in CI (.github/workflows/ci.yaml).
# One CVE id per line, each group with a comment: why it is accepted and when to revisit.
# `exp:` makes Trivy enforce the finding again after that date.
# Findings listed here are still reported in the Security tab via SARIF.

# --- client image: Go standard library inside the esbuild binary ---------------------
# Path: /app/node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild (esbuild 0.25.12, built with Go 1.23.12).
# esbuild only runs at dev/build time on our own sources; the affected stdlib packages
# (net/http, crypto/x509, archive/*, ...) are not reachable from untrusted input there.
# A newer esbuild requires vite 7+ (major upgrade), planned together with the nginx
# production image for the client — see docs/ai-guides/PROJECT-STATUS.md "Known Issues".
